1..9
ok 1 the incident: a directly-invoked non-executable script is reported NOEXEC
ok 2 control leg: the SAME crontab is clean once the exec bit is restored
ok 3 an interpreter in front means the exec bit is irrelevant — not reported
ok 4 bash-prefixed invocation is likewise not reported
ok 5 a relative fragment following a shell variable is not treated as a path
ok 6 an absolute path that does not exist is reported MISSING
ok 7 @reboot lines are parsed — their USER field sits in a different column
ok 8 commented-out lines are ignored
